\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Ah, holy Jesu, how hast Thou offended,
\par That man to judge Thee hath in hate pretended?
\par By foes derided, by Thine own rejected,
\par O most afflicted.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Who was the guilty? Who brought this upon Thee?
\par Alas, my treason, Jesu, hath undone Thee;
\par 'Twas I, Lord Jesu, I it was denied Thee:
\par I crucified Thee.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Lo, the good Shepherd for the sheep is offered;
\par The slave hath sinned, and the Son hath suffered;
\par For man's atonement, while he nothing heedeth,
\par God intercedeth.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. For me, kind Jesu, was Thy incarnation,
\par Thy mortal sorrow, and Thy life's oblation;
\par Thy death of anguish and Thy bitter passion,
\par For my salvation.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Therefore, kind Jesu, since I cannot pay Thee,
\par I do adore Thee, and will ever pray Thee,
\par Think on Thy pity and Thy love unswerving,
\par Not my deserving.
\par                           Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

